From 5d9050230b3cfb67775e8ff70ae44d44a71b813d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: cm36652: a driver for the Capella CM36652, and
 the Tab S2's sensor

The CM36652 is a colour light and proximity sensor at 0x60 with 16-bit
SMBus word registers; mainline's cm36651 is a different die (two
addresses, byte registers). The new IIO driver handles its light half:
red, green, blue and white counts, a shared integration time, and an
illuminance from the green channel. The proximity half is put in
shutdown at probe and resume, so its IR LED never runs. Register map and
normal configuration from Samsung's GPL driver for the chip; the colour
block matches the CM3323's. The integration time field is two bits (40,
80, 160 and 320 ms): on the SM-T715 under steady light the counts
doubled at each of those steps, and the CM3323's codes 4 and 5 read like
0 and 1. The lux scale (0.25168 lux per green count at 40 ms) is the
CM3323's published sensitivity, an approximation behind the cover glass.

The binding is capella,cm36652.yaml. On the Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE the
sensor sits on a bit-banged bus of its own (gpd4-1 SDA, gpd4-2 SCL, as
the stock device tree has it): the 64-bit-only fragment
exynos5433-gts28ltexx-als.dtsi.

On the SM-T715, 2026-11-28: the driver probes, reads about 20 lux in a
room, and the image's t715-autobrightness follows it.
---
